{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Therefore. Behold, I lay.</b> The descriptive noun is from the heavy [pa'el] conjugation, on the pattern of אבד, and behold, יוצא is like it. And I praised the dead (Ecclesiastes 4:2):" "<b>A tested stone.</b> Like עופל ובוחן (Isaiah 34:14) [n: Ibn Ezra's citation reads Isaiah 34:14, but עופל does not appear there; the reference is likely to a different verse or reflects a variant tradition], and the meaning is that Zion shall be exalted above the king of Assyria:" "<b>Corner of preciousness, foundation.</b> The first is a noun like היסוד, and יקרת is in construct state to it, and the second מוסד is a participle from the heavy [hitpa'el/huf'al] conjugation added, on the pattern of מוצב ארצה; therefore the samekh has a dagesh to absorb the doubling:" "<b>Believes, will not hasten.</b> For it will yet be many days before this prophecy comes [to pass]:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:38.498105733Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}